## Dataset

The model expects a CSV with the following columns. A synthetic dataset with this schema is generated automatically when no file is present, so the project runs out of the box. To use real institutional data, place a CSV with the same columns at `data/raw/student_placement.csv`.

| Column | Type | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `gender` | categorical | Male / Female / Other |
| `branch` | categorical | Academic branch (CSE, IT, ECE, EE, ME, CE) |
| `extracurricular` | categorical | Yes / No |
| `cgpa` | numeric | Cumulative GPA on a 10-point scale |
| `tenth_percentage` | numeric | Class X score (%) |
| `twelfth_percentage` | numeric | Class XII score (%) |
| `backlogs` | numeric | Number of active backlogs |
| `internships` | numeric | Number of completed internships |
| `projects` | numeric | Number of projects completed |
| `certifications` | numeric | Number of professional certifications |
| `hackathons` | numeric | Number of hackathons attended |
| `coding_score` | numeric | Coding assessment score (0–100) |
| `aptitude_score` | numeric | Aptitude test score (0–100) |
| `communication_score` | numeric | Communication assessment score (0–100) |
| `study_hours_per_day` | numeric | Average self-study hours per day (may be missing) |
| `attendance_percentage` | numeric | Attendance (%) (may be missing) |
| `placed` | target (0/1) | 1 if the student received a placement offer |

Missing numeric values are imputed with the median, and missing categories with the most frequent value.

> **Note on the synthetic data.** The generator encodes plausible relationships (for example, CGPA, coding skill, internships, and backlogs increase placement odds) but it is not real institutional data. Results on synthetic data demonstrate the pipeline; they should not be read as evidence about real students.

